  "observations": [
    "Neither direct SDK vendor-loader trial produced the nonce-bound constructor receipt. No native-only capability entry or acquisition is qualified.",
    "QN90A emitted EFL diagnostics and exited 255. Exact loader analysis places EFL initialization after the preload loop. The matching vendor bundle decoder confirmed the fixed preload array; loading the probe did not reach its terminating constructor.",
    "S90D emitted a runtime-directory diagnostic and terminated with signal 9 during the bounded trial. The fixed process watchdog covered the expected loader; later inspection proved process absence. No receipt or precise loader failure cause was observed.",
    "Both target libbundle implementations decoded the fixed host bundle and re-encoded identical bytes through a private managed diagnostic. Temporary diagnostics were removed.",
    "Both own WGT probe files are package-labeled regular files on writable VDFS. Existing signed-TPK research already distinguishes package signing from native executable verification; no TPK workaround is claimed.",
    "The first full macOS Python run hit an existing deadline-test process-group PermissionError. A focused deadline recheck and the full 399-test rerun passed."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No private read-only code view, persistent file capability, loader registration, SMACK rule, HOME/XDG override, firmware change, reboot or standby was introduced by the entry experiment.",
    "The managed capability-entry bridge, identity children, acquisition fallback, worker fallback and SDK recovery utility remain required or retained as before.",
    "Binary-parser evidence and codec agreement do not establish a successful native entry. Code mapping and actual vendor-loader credentials must be proven before acquisition integration.",
    "Private identities, vendor binaries, raw receipts, signed packages and detailed process/watchdog evidence remain outside Git."
  ]
